# What this file does, and what it does not do.
#
# GitHub asks the maintainer to review every pull request from someone else (not drafts) that changes a path below,
# and marks those paths in the diff. That is all. No ruleset of this repository requires a code owner's approval (a
# single maintainer cannot approve their own pull requests), so this file enforces nothing and is not a security
# control. In a fork, the owner named here has no effect: change it to your own reviewer or delete the lines.
#
# The paths are the ones a reviewer must read closely: CI and the hermetic test guard (red-team F10), the files that
# instruct AI coding assistants (root Markdown files, root dot files and folders, the skills under .agents/, and
# every AGENTS.md at any depth), the scripts that install, update and release StackVend (scripts/, including the
# release keys in scripts/release/allowed_signers), and the platform upgrader.
/.github/                                @asaslaw
/conftest.py                             @asaslaw
/pytest.ini                              @asaslaw
/tests/conftest.py                       @asaslaw
/tests/hermetic_guard.py                 @asaslaw
/tests/hermetic_known_leaks.py           @asaslaw
/*.md                                    @asaslaw
/.*                                      @asaslaw
AGENTS.md                                @asaslaw
/.agents/                                @asaslaw
/scripts/                                @asaslaw
/infra/platform/upgrade_step0/           @asaslaw
/infra/platform/platform_upgrader.tf     @asaslaw
